                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed6eedc1-b749-3bd7-bf5d-cd3c25ea9020",
                        "entry_id": "0e47a786-6148-369a-9c1a-cf18cbaf4fea",
                        "glosses": [
                            "prosta, do której dąży dana krzywa lub wykres danej funkcji"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "05b82619-0910-460e-8faf-84b0dff78cab",
                                "sense_id": "ed6eedc1-b749-3bd7-bf5d-cd3c25ea9020",
                                "text": "Oś rzędnych jest asymptotą cotangensa."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb43b39b-8e5c-4534-b9f0-9a69f16e9003",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e47a786-6148-369a-9c1a-cf18cbaf4fea",
                        "source_sense_id": "ed6eedc1-b749-3bd7-bf5d-cd3c25ea9020",
                        "target_lang_word": "asymptote",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "asymptote",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29b76317-4f09-338d-b611-3fe14dee0206",
                                        "entry_id": "6153e64f-fdd1-3a58-8e38-b86ac92b0daa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A straight line which a curve approaches arbitrarily closely as it goes to infinity. The limit of the curve; its tangent \\\"at infinity\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f57311be-32dd-4975-a1ae-8d90b6da5e2f",
                                                "sense_id": "29b76317-4f09-338d-b611-3fe14dee0206",
                                                "text": "The King rushed forward with all his cruel coordinates and mean values, stumbled into a dark forest of roots and logarithms, had to backtrack, then encountered the beast on a field of irrational numbers (F₁) and smote it so grievously that it fell two decimal places and lost an epsilon, but the beast slid around an asymptote and hid in an n-dimensional orthogonal phase space, underwent expansion and came out, fuming factorially, and fell upon the King and hurt him passing sore."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa2889a0-5718-3974-ad53-dcab3a722f57",
                                        "entry_id": "6153e64f-fdd1-3a58-8e38-b86ac92b0daa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything which comes near to but never meets something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a8b5edf-e6c9-4184-9071-c0a8196b59c3",
                                                "sense_id": "fa2889a0-5718-3974-ad53-dcab3a722f57",
                                                "text": "Language, in relation to thought, must ever be regarded as an asymptote."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "asymptote",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "260e403c-393a-3184-84a1-df43444bb879",
                                        "entry_id": "47a62afc-265f-3825-bbe9-f07af0faff96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To approach, but never quite touch, a straight line, as something goes to infinity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e1847f8-7618-426a-b7da-d559b22120d5",
                                                "sense_id": "260e403c-393a-3184-84a1-df43444bb879",
                                                "text": "2006: Neil deGrasse Tyson, The Perimeter of Ignorance\nAs you become more scientific, yes, the religiosity drops off, but it asymptotes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "81b27511-2c3e-4965-9c6c-d675ac3dbd24",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e47a786-6148-369a-9c1a-cf18cbaf4fea",
                        "source_sense_id": "ed6eedc1-b749-3bd7-bf5d-cd3c25ea9020",
                        "target_lang_word": "asymptota",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ace12a9-ed99-4c5b-83b3-0f69c07bc4f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e47a786-6148-369a-9c1a-cf18cbaf4fea",
                        "source_sense_id": "ed6eedc1-b749-3bd7-bf5d-cd3c25ea9020",
                        "target_lang_word": "asymptote",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "asymptote",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "02d3f444-bc71-32c9-9b64-57a3c9fe694e",
                                        "entry_id": "57d86925-7281-3c4f-bdce-9c3799fde430",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Se dit d’une droite, et par extension d’une courbe simple, vers laquelle d’autres courbes s’approchent, à l’infini, à une distance plus petite que toute quantité positive fixée préalablement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "analytic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "asymptote",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a8ed655-50e2-36c8-a224-17c837ce6665",
                                        "entry_id": "55a08661-7622-3be8-98aa-27a3a11a8a4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Droite ou courbe se rapprochant indéfiniment d’une autre courbe à l’infini ; en pratique, une asymptote est le plus souvent une droite dont la valeur de l’une des coordonnées (abscisse ou ordonnée) est constante, c’est-à-dire indépendante de la valeur de la coordonnée de l’autre axe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "analytic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e650834-c161-42aa-988f-7b52f0ff7abe",
                                                "sense_id": "3a8ed655-50e2-36c8-a224-17c837ce6665",
                                                "text": "Les hyperboles redondantes ainsi appelées par Newton parce qu’elles surpassent les sections coniques quant au nombre des branches hyperboliques, sont caractérisées par l’existence de trois points hyperboliques, et par conséquent de trois asymptotes de directions deux à deux différentes.\nCes trois asymptotes forment un triangle qui peut se réduire à un point."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4023437-6da6-4cbf-8ad4-31f9e3b350a4",
                                                "sense_id": "3a8ed655-50e2-36c8-a224-17c837ce6665",
                                                "text": "—Approcher toujours, n’arriver jamais ; telle est la loi. La civilisation est une asymptote."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
